msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:890
msgid "`cir.asm` (::cir::InlineAsmOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:892
msgid "The `cir.asm` operation represents C/C++ asm inline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:894
msgid ""
"CIR constraints strings follow the same rules that are established for the C "
"level assembler constraints with several differences caused by "
"clang::AsmStmt processing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:898
msgid "Thus, numbers that appears in the constraint string may also refer to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:899
msgid "the output variable index referenced by the input operands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:900
msgid "the index of early-clobber operand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:902
msgid ""
"`operand_attrs` has one entry per operand, in operand order: a unit "
"attribute marks a memory operand (printed as `maybe_memory`) and an empty "
"dictionary marks any other operand. The operands themselves are stored as "
"VariadicOfVariadic in the following order: output, input and then in/out "
"operands. When several output operands are present, the result type may be "
"represented as an anonymous record type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:909
msgid ""
"The `convergent` attribute marks asm that may contain convergent operations, "
"so it must not be moved across divergent control flow."
msgstr ""

