"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>poison</code></td><td>::mlir::UnitAttr</td><td>unit attribute</"
"td></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>operand_segments</code></td><td>::mlir::DenseI32ArrayAttr</"
"td><td>i32 dense array attribute</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`succ_operands`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`successors`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7518
msgid "`cir.indirect_goto` (::cir::IndirectGotoOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7520
msgid "_Symbolic indirect goto_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7528
msgid ""
"Transfers control to the block whose address is held in `$addr`, the void-"
"pointer value of a `goto *expr;` (the GNU computed-goto extension). Like "
"`cir.goto`, it is symbolic: it references no successor block, so it is valid "
"inside any region even before `FlattenCFG` merges nested scopes. "
"`GotoSolver` runs after `FlattenCFG` and rewrites each `cir.indirect_goto` "
"into a `cir.br` to a shared block holding a `cir.indirect_br` over every "
"address-taken label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7553
msgid "`cir.init_catch_param` (::cir::InitCatchParamOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7555
msgid "_Initialize a catch parameter from the exception pointer_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7564
msgid ""
"`cir.init_catch_param` represents copying or otherwise materializing the "
"caught exception object into the local catch parameter variable. It takes "
"the exception pointer returned by `cir.begin_catch` and the address of the "
"alloca created for the catch parameter, and has no result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7569
msgid ""
"This operation is target-independent. It is replaced during EHABI lowering "
"with the appropriate target/ABI-specific sequence (for example, the Itanium "
"C++ ABI may emit a load and store for scalar/pointer catch types, an "
"aggregate copy for record types, or a call to a copy constructor when one is "
"required)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7575
msgid ""
"A catch parameter that is a reference to a pointer uses the "
"`reference_to_record_pointer` kind when the pointer's source-level pointee "
"type is a record (class, struct, or union), and `reference_to_pointer` "
"otherwise. A reference to any other type uses `reference`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7580
msgid ""
"A `reference_to_pointer` or `non_trivial_copy` operation requires its catch "
"handler to start with a `cir.construct_catch_param` of the same kind on the "
"same parameter. When the handler starts with a `cir.construct_catch_param` "
"on the parameter of the operation, the two must have the same kind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7597
msgid ""
"<table>\n"
"<tr><th>Attribute</th><th>MLIR Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n"
"<tr><td><code>kind</code></td><td>::cir::InitCatchKindAttr</td><td>allowed "
"i32 cases: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7</td></tr>\n"
"</table>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7611
msgid "`cir.insert_member` (::cir::InsertMemberOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7613
msgid "_Overwrite the value of a member of a record value_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7622
msgid ""
"The `cir.insert_member` operation overwrites the value of a particular "
"member in the input record, and returns the modified record. The result of "
"this operation is equal to the input record, except for the member specified "
"by `index_attr` whose value is equal to the given value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7627
msgid "This operation is named after the LLVM instruction `insertvalue`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7629
msgid "Currently `cir.insert_member` does not work on unions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7677
msgid "`cir.is_constant` (::cir::IsConstantOp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7679
msgid "_Test for manifest compile-time constant_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7687
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the argument is known to be a manifest compile-time "
"constant otherwise returns `false`. If the argument is a constant expression "
"which refers to a global (the address of which _is_ a constant, but not "
"manifest during the compile), then the intrinsic evaluates to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:7692
msgid ""
"This is used to represent `__builtin_constant_p` in cases where the argument "
"isn't known to be constant during initial translation of the source code but "
"might be proven to be constant after later optimizations."
msgstr ""

