#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16240
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.cleanup_token`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16242
msgid ""
"`!cir.cleanup_token` is an opaque type used to track cleanup handling state "
"in flattened CIR. It is returned by `cir.begin_cleanup` and consumed by "
"`cir.end_cleanup`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16246
msgid ""
"This token ensures that cleanup regions are properly paired and allows the "
"ABI lowering pass to generate appropriate cleanup handling code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16250
msgid "ComplexType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16252
msgid "_CIR complex type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16262
msgid ""
"CIR type that represents a C complex number. `cir.complex` models the C type "
"`T _Complex`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16265
msgid "`cir.complex` type is not directly mapped to `std::complex`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16267
msgid ""
"The type models complex values, per C99 6.2.5p11. It supports the C99 "
"complex float types as well as the GCC integer complex extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16270
msgid ""
"The parameter `elementType` gives the type of the real and imaginary part of "
"the complex number. `elementType` must be either a CIR integer type or a CIR "
"floating-point type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16285
msgid "DataMemberType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16287
msgid "_CIR type that represents a pointer-to-data-member in C++_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16298
msgid ""
"`cir.data_member` models a pointer-to-data-member in C++. Values of this "
"type are essentially offsets of the pointed-to member within one of its "
"containing record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "member_ty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "any type from the CIR dialect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "class_ty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "`cir::RecordType`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16309
msgid "DoubleType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16311
msgid "_CIR double-precision 64-bit float type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16313
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.double`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16315
msgid ""
"A 64-bit floating-point type whose format is IEEE-754 `binary64`. It "
"represents the types `double', '_Float64`, `std::float64_t`, and `_Float32x` "
"in C and C++.  This is the underlying type for `long double` on some "
"platforms, including Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16321
msgid "EhTokenType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16323
msgid "_CIR exception handling token type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16325
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.eh_token`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16327
msgid ""
"`!cir.eh_token` is an opaque type used to track exception handling state in "
"flattened CIR. It is returned by `cir.eh.initiate` and passed to "
"`cir.eh.dispatch`, `cir.begin_cleanup`, and `cir.begin_catch` operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16331
msgid ""
"This token represents an in-flight exception and is used during ABI-lowering "
"to generate the appropriate exception handling code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16335
msgid "FP16Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16337
msgid "_CIR half-precision 16-bit float type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16339
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.f16`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16341
msgid ""
"A 16-bit floating-point type whose format is IEEE-754 `binary16`. It "
"represents the types '_Float16` and `std::float16_t` in C and C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16345
msgid "FP80Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16347
msgid "_CIR x87 80-bit float type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16349
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.f80`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16351
msgid ""
"An 80-bit floating-point type in the x87 extended precision format.  The "
"size and alignment of the type are both 128 bits, even though only 80 of "
"those bits are used.  This is the underlying type for `long double` on Linux "
"x86 platforms, and it is available as an extension in some implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16357
msgid "FP128Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16359
msgid "_CIR quad-precision 128-bit float type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16361
msgid "Syntax: `!cir.f128`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16363
msgid ""
"A 128-bit floating-point type whose format is IEEE-754 `binary128`. It "
"represents the types `_Float128` and `std::float128_t` in C and C++, and the "
"extension `__float128` in some implementations.  This is the underlying type "
"for `long double` on some platforms including Linux Arm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16369
msgid "FuncType"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16371
msgid "_CIR function type_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:16383
msgid ""
"The `!cir.func` is a function type. It consists of an optional return type, "
"a list of parameter types and can optionally be variadic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CIR/CIRDialect.md:0
msgid "inputs"
msgstr ""

